cartridge "STIX!/AHOY!/1989"

' STIX!
' A ColecoVision game based on "STIX!", Ahoy! February 1989 (Commodore
' 128 BASIC 7.0, disk ahoy1989-02; no author named on the disk or in the
' listing). Made for Amy Studio by Claude (an AI made by Anthropic), 2026,
' in Amy by Amy Bienvenu.
'
' Four logical puzzles about the placement of eight sticks, drawn here as
' matches standing in holes on a black board:
'
' 1 LINEARSTIX: nine holes in a row, four red matches on the left, four
'   blue on the right, the middle hole empty. Red moves right, blue moves
'   left, only forward: a step into the next hole, or a jump over one match
'   into the hole behind it. Swap the two sides.
' 2 TRISTIXULAR: ten holes in a triangle (rows of 4, 3, 2 and 1), eight
'   matches. Pick a match, then an empty hole two along a row or two along
'   a diagonal with a match between: it jumps, and the jumped match goes.
'   Leave only one.
' 3 INTERSTIXTION: a cross of two lines of nine holes sharing the middle
'   one. Two red matches at the left go right, two green at the top go
'   down, two blue at the right go left, two yellow at the bottom go up, in
'   that order, one move each turn (a step or a jump, forward only). Bring
'   every pair to the far end of its line. A colour that cannot move when
'   its turn comes loses the game.
' 4 TRANSTIXION: eight matches (3, 2, 3) on seven lines. Choose a line: its
'   matches all change colour, red > yellow > green > blue > red. Make
'   them all red.
'
' From the original (orig/stix.bas, read from the listing; C-128 programs
' do not run in the toolbox's emulator): the four boards and their holes,
' the moves and jumps, the win tests, TRISTIXULAR's first match in the
' middle of row 2 and seven more dealt at random, INTERSTIXTION's turn
' order (right, down, left, up), TRANSTIXION's seven lines and colour
' order and its 20 random line changes to mix the colours, the names, the
' objectives (the title's scrolling text, here a page before each puzzle),
' the win screen ("CONGRATULATIONS ... WE HAVE A WINNER IN ... AND THE
' CROWD GOES WILD"), starting over (the C-128's space bar) at any time.
'
' Improvements and liberties: the sticks are matches on a black board with
' guide dots between the holes; a match hops in a smooth arc as a sprite
' and lands back as tiles (never more than three sprites); a pointer that
' glides (LINEARSTIX, TRISTIXULAR) and lit holes (the chosen match, the
' chosen line) instead of the C-128's blinking sprites; TRISTIXULAR deals
' only positions that can be won (half of the C-128's could not: model.mjs
' searched them all; the C-128 only redealt when the three corners were
' full); a game that can no longer be won ends with a message (NO MOVES
' LEFT; in INTERSTIXTION the colour that cannot move loses, as the
' objective says) where the C-128 waited for the space bar; a move counter
' and the session's best for each puzzle; TRANSTIXION is never dealt
' already solved; TRANSTIXION's colour routines (listing lines 1670-1720)
' are damaged on the disk image: rebuilt as one step forward for each
' match of the line (the order the objective gives); TRISTIXULAR's
' pointer moves with up/down/left/right and the diagonals (the C-128
' used only the diagonals and left/right). INTERSTIXTION shows whose turn
' it is. New tune and sounds; the title letters are matches.
'
' Controls: joystick only (either controller). Title: up and down choose,
' a button starts. LINEARSTIX: left/right move the pointer, the left
' button moves the match. TRISTIXULAR: the stick moves the pointer, the
' left button picks a match, then on an empty hole makes it jump.
' INTERSTIXTION: the stick chooses between the two matches whose turn it
' is, the left button moves it. TRANSTIXION: the stick chooses a line, the
' left button changes its colours. Right button: start the puzzle over;
' held for a second and a half: back to the title.
'
' House rules: text in columns 2-29, rows 1-22; tiles from code 128; the
' frame loop is protected from the NMI; screens drawn with the NMI off
' after a wait, display off. Music first in the sound table, effects after;
' the title tune is played once. `set sprite count` after every `clear
' sprites`. Own xorshift random numbers.
'
' Workarounds for Amy bugs sack-div-in-sum, sack-print-bcd-var-index, sack-bcd-element-carry removed 2026-11-01.

